# NOLQERA Error Resolution & Prevention Guide

This document captures all the errors encountered during the implementation and integration of the Semantic Search engine, their root causes, step-by-step solutions, and best practices to prevent them in the future.

---

## 1. Accidental Deletion of Source Directories
### Error
Files under `nolqera/intelligence/semantic_similarity/` were deleted, resulting in broken imports and test execution failures.

### Root Cause
An accidental directory removal or command sequence deleted the existing package directory before creating the new `semantic_search` directory.

### How to Fix
Restore the deleted folder tracking from the Git index:
```powershell
git restore nolqera/intelligence/semantic_similarity
```

### How to Avoid in Future
* **Review Working Trees**: Run `git status` before execution of destructive commands.
* **Safer File Management**: Use Git-integrated commands or IDE workspaces to perform moves and renames rather than shell commands (`rm`, `Remove-Item`) to prevent unintended deletions.

